%S A400453 1,3,4,5,6,12,8,9,10,18,12,20,14,24,24,21,18,30,20,30,32,36,24,36,26,
%T A400453 42,28,40,30,72,32,45,48,54,48,50,38,60,56,54,42,96,44,60,60,72,48,84,
%U A400453 50,78,72,70,54,84,72,72,80,90,60,120,62,96,80,93,84,144,68,90,96,144
%N A400453 The sum of divisors d of n such that gcd(d, n/d) is a powerful number (A001694).
%C A400453 Differs from A365172 at n = 64, 128, 192, 256, 320, 384, 448, ... .
%C A400453 The number of these divisors is A369310(n).
%H A400453 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A400453/b400453.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A400453 Multiplicative with a(p) = p + 1, a(p^2) = p^2 + 1, and a(p^e) = (p^2-p+1)*(p^(e-1)-1)/(p-1) for e >= 3.
%F A400453 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s-1) * zeta(s) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^(2*s-1) + 1/p^(4*s-2)).
%F A400453 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ c * n^2 / 2, where c = zeta(2)*zeta(6)*zeta(9)/(zeta(3)*zeta(18)) = zeta(2) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^3 + 1/p^6) = 1.394956282534702944... .
%F A400453 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s-1) * zeta(s) * zeta(4*s-2) * zeta(6*s-3) / (zeta(2*s-1) * zeta(12*s-6)). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Sep 27 2026
%t A400453 f[p_, e_] := (p^2-p+1)*(p^(e-1)-1)/(p-1); f[p_, 1] := p + 1; f[p_, 2] := p^2 + 1;
%t A400453 a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 100]
%o A400453 (PARI) a(n) = {my(f = factor(n)); prod(i = 1, #f~, p = f[i,1]; e = f[i,2]; if(e == 1, p+1, if(e == 2, p^2 + 1, (p^2-p+1)*(p^(e-1)-1)/(p-1))));}
%Y A400453 Cf. A001694, A369310, A400390.
%Y A400453 Cf. A002117, A013661, A013664, A013667, A013676.
%Y A400453 The sum of divisors d of n such that gcd(d, n/d) is: A034448 (1), A069184 (odd), A107749 (power of 2), A365172 (square), A365174 (exponentially odd), A365209 (3-smooth), A365211 (5-rough), this sequence (powerful).
%K A400453 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A400453 1,2
